Ok maybe I misunderstood something.
I thought that f(race) would give me a random intercept, whereas f(race, variable) would give me a random slope ?

What I actually want to do is tranlate an lmer mixed effects equation to inla. The lmer equation would be like so:

> case.control ~ 1 + variable + (variable | country)
>

1 + variable is an interecept + fixed effect of variable
(variable | country) is the random effect of variable across the level country and is implicit to mean  (1 + variable | country) so in includes a random intercept (unless you supress it)

I thought that inla for a continuous variable the equivalent would be:

> case.control ~ 1 + variable + f(country, variable)
>
But for a categorial variable I thought I had to use dummy variables. Perhaps I have simply confused myself ?

